IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je54-nouns`
IMPORT `je54-vintage`
IMPORT `je54-art11-powers`

-- je54-tests-art11-powers: Articles 11 and 11A.  Expected values were written from the text of the Articles in each of the seven deposited versions before this module was run.
-- V1 has Article 11(1) to 11(4) and no 11A; V2a to V2f have 11(1), 11(2), the inert placeholders "(3) [12]" and "(4) [13]", and 11A.  The same scenario is put to every text.

`text V1` MEANS `V1, 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021`
`text V2a` MEANS `V2a, 28 September 2021 to 30 January 2022`
`text V2b` MEANS `V2b, 31 January 2022 to 31 August 2022`
`text V2c` MEANS `V2c, 1 September 2022 to 10 January 2024`
`text V2d` MEANS `V2d, 11 January 2024 to 23 November 2025`
`text V2e` MEANS `V2e, 24 November 2025 to 18 June 2026`
`text V2f` MEANS `V2f, 19 June 2026 to current`
`text inferred` MEANS `the inferred text from 28 March 2003 to 31 December 2018`
`text none` MEANS `no text before 28 March 2003`

§ `Article 11(1): from time to time as occasion requires`

#ASSERT `Article 11(1): the power may be exercised or the duty must be performed on this occasion` `text V1` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 11(1): the power may be exercised or the duty must be performed on this occasion` `text V2a` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 11(1): the power may be exercised or the duty must be performed on this occasion` `text V2b` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 11(1): the power may be exercised or the duty must be performed on this occasion` `text V2c` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 11(1): the power may be exercised or the duty must be performed on this occasion` `text V2d` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 11(1): the power may be exercised or the duty must be performed on this occasion` `text V2e` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 11(1): the power may be exercised or the duty must be performed on this occasion` `text V2f` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 11(1): the power may be exercised or the duty must be performed on this occasion` `text V1` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 11(1): the power may be exercised or the duty must be performed on this occasion` `text V2a` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 11(1): the power may be exercised or the duty must be performed on this occasion` `text V2b` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 11(1): the power may be exercised or the duty must be performed on this occasion` `text V2c` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 11(1): the power may be exercised or the duty must be performed on this occasion` `text V2d` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 11(1): the power may be exercised or the duty must be performed on this occasion` `text V2e` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 11(1): the power may be exercised or the duty must be performed on this occasion` `text V2f` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 11(1): the power may be exercised or the duty must be performed on this occasion` `text V1` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 11(1): the power may be exercised or the duty must be performed on this occasion` `text V2f` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11(1): the power may be exercised or the duty must be performed on this occasion` `text V1` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 11(1) deals only where an enactment confers a power or imposes a duty"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11(1): the power may be exercised or the duty must be performed on this occasion` `text V2f` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
        BECAUSE "a contrary intention appears: Article 11(1) does not say how often the power may be exercised or the duty performed"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11(1): the power may be exercised or the duty must be performed on this occasion` `text inferred` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11(1): the power may be exercised or the duty must be performed on this occasion` `text none` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"

§ `Article 11(2): the holder of an office as such`

#ASSERT `Article 11(2): who exercises the power or performs the duty of the office` `text V1` TRUE "the Bailiff" FALSE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS "the Bailiff"
#ASSERT `Article 11(2): who exercises the power or performs the duty of the office` `text V2a` TRUE "the Bailiff" FALSE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS "the Bailiff"
#ASSERT `Article 11(2): who exercises the power or performs the duty of the office` `text V2b` TRUE "the Bailiff" FALSE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS "the Bailiff"
#ASSERT `Article 11(2): who exercises the power or performs the duty of the office` `text V2c` TRUE "the Bailiff" FALSE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS "the Bailiff"
#ASSERT `Article 11(2): who exercises the power or performs the duty of the office` `text V2d` TRUE "the Bailiff" FALSE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS "the Bailiff"
#ASSERT `Article 11(2): who exercises the power or performs the duty of the office` `text V2e` TRUE "the Bailiff" FALSE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS "the Bailiff"
#ASSERT `Article 11(2): who exercises the power or performs the duty of the office` `text V2f` TRUE "the Bailiff" FALSE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS "the Bailiff"
#ASSERT `Article 11(2): who exercises the power or performs the duty of the office` `text V1` TRUE "the Bailiff" TRUE (JUST "the Deputy Bailiff") FALSE EQUALS "the Deputy Bailiff"
#ASSERT `Article 11(2): who exercises the power or performs the duty of the office` `text V2a` TRUE "the Bailiff" TRUE (JUST "the Deputy Bailiff") FALSE EQUALS "the Deputy Bailiff"
#ASSERT `Article 11(2): who exercises the power or performs the duty of the office` `text V2b` TRUE "the Bailiff" TRUE (JUST "the Deputy Bailiff") FALSE EQUALS "the Deputy Bailiff"
#ASSERT `Article 11(2): who exercises the power or performs the duty of the office` `text V2c` TRUE "the Bailiff" TRUE (JUST "the Deputy Bailiff") FALSE EQUALS "the Deputy Bailiff"
#ASSERT `Article 11(2): who exercises the power or performs the duty of the office` `text V2d` TRUE "the Bailiff" TRUE (JUST "the Deputy Bailiff") FALSE EQUALS "the Deputy Bailiff"
#ASSERT `Article 11(2): who exercises the power or performs the duty of the office` `text V2e` TRUE "the Bailiff" TRUE (JUST "the Deputy Bailiff") FALSE EQUALS "the Deputy Bailiff"
#ASSERT `Article 11(2): who exercises the power or performs the duty of the office` `text V2f` TRUE "the Bailiff" TRUE (JUST "the Deputy Bailiff") FALSE EQUALS "the Deputy Bailiff"
-- A performer who is named while the holder is present is not used: the holder acts.
#ASSERT `Article 11(2): who exercises the power or performs the duty of the office` `text V2c` TRUE "the Bailiff" FALSE (JUST "the Deputy Bailiff") FALSE EQUALS "the Bailiff"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11(2): who exercises the power or performs the duty of the office` `text V1` TRUE "the Bailiff" TRUE NOTHING FALSE
        BECAUSE "the holder of the office is absent or incapacitated and nobody is performing the duty of the office: Article 11(2) names no one"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11(2): who exercises the power or performs the duty of the office` `text V2f` FALSE "the Bailiff" FALSE NOTHING FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 11(2) deals only where an enactment confers a power or imposes a duty on the holder of an office as such"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11(2): who exercises the power or performs the duty of the office` `text V2a` TRUE "the Bailiff" TRUE (JUST "the Deputy Bailiff") TRUE
        BECAUSE "a contrary intention appears: Article 11(2) does not say who exercises the power or performs the duty"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11(2): who exercises the power or performs the duty of the office` `text inferred` TRUE "the Bailiff" FALSE NOTHING FALSE
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"

§ `Article 11(3): a power to pass an enactment includes a power to repeal, rescind, amend or vary it (V1 only)`

#ASSERT `Article 11(3): the power to pass the other enactment includes the power` `text V1` TRUE `to repeal it` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 11(3): the power to pass the other enactment includes the power` `text V1` TRUE `to rescind it` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 11(3): the power to pass the other enactment includes the power` `text V1` TRUE `to amend it` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 11(3): the power to pass the other enactment includes the power` `text V1` TRUE `to vary it` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 11(3): the power to pass the other enactment includes the power` `text V1` TRUE `some other act on it` FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11(3): the power to pass the other enactment includes the power` `text V2a` TRUE `to amend it` FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 11(3) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 is deleted from 28 September 2021 (L.8/2021); it is not in the text of the Law in force on this day"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11(3): the power to pass the other enactment includes the power` `text V2b` TRUE `to amend it` FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 11(3) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 is deleted from 28 September 2021 (L.8/2021); it is not in the text of the Law in force on this day"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11(3): the power to pass the other enactment includes the power` `text V2c` TRUE `to amend it` FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 11(3) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 is deleted from 28 September 2021 (L.8/2021); it is not in the text of the Law in force on this day"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11(3): the power to pass the other enactment includes the power` `text V2d` TRUE `to amend it` FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 11(3) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 is deleted from 28 September 2021 (L.8/2021); it is not in the text of the Law in force on this day"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11(3): the power to pass the other enactment includes the power` `text V2e` TRUE `to amend it` FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 11(3) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 is deleted from 28 September 2021 (L.8/2021); it is not in the text of the Law in force on this day"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11(3): the power to pass the other enactment includes the power` `text V2f` TRUE `to amend it` FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 11(3) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 is deleted from 28 September 2021 (L.8/2021); it is not in the text of the Law in force on this day"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11(3): the power to pass the other enactment includes the power` `text V1` FALSE `to amend it` FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 11(3) deals only where an enactment confers a power to pass any other enactment"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11(3): the power to pass the other enactment includes the power` `text V1` TRUE `to amend it` TRUE
        BECAUSE "a contrary intention appears: Article 11(3) does not say what the power to pass the other enactment then includes"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11(3): the power to pass the other enactment includes the power` `text inferred` TRUE `to amend it` FALSE
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"

§ `Article 11(4): the ways a power to make an enactment may be exercised (V1 only; enactment passed after 28th March 2003)`

-- Each of the ten ways the Article lists, for an enactment passed on 29 March 2003 (the first day after 28th March 2003).
#ASSERT `Article 11(4): the power may be exercised in the way` `text V1` TRUE (YMD 2003 3 29) `in relation to all cases to which the power extends` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 11(4): the power may be exercised in the way` `text V1` TRUE (YMD 2003 3 29) `in relation to all those cases subject to specified exceptions` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 11(4): the power may be exercised in the way` `text V1` TRUE (YMD 2003 3 29) `in relation to any specified cases or classes of case` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 11(4): the power may be exercised in the way` `text V1` TRUE (YMD 2003 3 29) `so as to make the full provision to which the power extends` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 11(4): the power may be exercised in the way` `text V1` TRUE (YMD 2003 3 29) `so as to make any lesser provision, whether by way of exception or otherwise` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 11(4): the power may be exercised in the way` `text V1` TRUE (YMD 2003 3 29) `so as to make the same provision for all cases in which the power is exercised` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 11(4): the power may be exercised in the way` `text V1` TRUE (YMD 2003 3 29) `so as to make different provision for different cases or classes of case` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 11(4): the power may be exercised in the way` `text V1` TRUE (YMD 2003 3 29) `so as to make different provision as respects the same case or class of case for different purposes of the enactment` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 11(4): the power may be exercised in the way` `text V1` TRUE (YMD 2003 3 29) `so as to make any such provision unconditionally` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 11(4): the power may be exercised in the way` `text V1` TRUE (YMD 2003 3 29) `so as to make any such provision subject to a specified condition` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 11(4): the power may be exercised in the way` `text V1` TRUE (YMD 2003 3 29) `in some other way` FALSE
-- The date edge: passed after 28th March 2003 is passed on 29 March 2003 or later; passed on 28 March 2003 itself, or before, is not.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 11(4): the power may be exercised in the way` `text V1` TRUE (YMD 2003 3 28) `in relation to all cases to which the power extends` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 11(4): the power may be exercised in the way` `text V1` TRUE (YMD 2003 3 27) `in relation to all cases to which the power extends` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 11(4): the power may be exercised in the way` `text V1` TRUE (YMD 1954 8 21) `in relation to all cases to which the power extends` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 11(4): the power may be exercised in the way` `text V1` TRUE (YMD 2003 3 30) `so as to make any such provision unconditionally` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 11(4): the power may be exercised in the way` `text V1` TRUE (YMD 2019 1 1) `so as to make any such provision unconditionally` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 11(4): the power may be exercised in the way` `text V1` TRUE (YMD 2021 9 27) `so as to make any such provision unconditionally` FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11(4): the power may be exercised in the way` `text V2a` TRUE (YMD 2010 1 1) `in relation to all cases to which the power extends` FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 11(4) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 is deleted from 28 September 2021 (L.8/2021); it is not in the text of the Law in force on this day"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11(4): the power may be exercised in the way` `text V2b` TRUE (YMD 2010 1 1) `in relation to all cases to which the power extends` FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 11(4) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 is deleted from 28 September 2021 (L.8/2021); it is not in the text of the Law in force on this day"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11(4): the power may be exercised in the way` `text V2c` TRUE (YMD 2010 1 1) `in relation to all cases to which the power extends` FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 11(4) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 is deleted from 28 September 2021 (L.8/2021); it is not in the text of the Law in force on this day"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11(4): the power may be exercised in the way` `text V2d` TRUE (YMD 2010 1 1) `in relation to all cases to which the power extends` FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 11(4) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 is deleted from 28 September 2021 (L.8/2021); it is not in the text of the Law in force on this day"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11(4): the power may be exercised in the way` `text V2e` TRUE (YMD 2010 1 1) `in relation to all cases to which the power extends` FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 11(4) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 is deleted from 28 September 2021 (L.8/2021); it is not in the text of the Law in force on this day"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11(4): the power may be exercised in the way` `text V2f` TRUE (YMD 2010 1 1) `in relation to all cases to which the power extends` FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 11(4) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 is deleted from 28 September 2021 (L.8/2021); it is not in the text of the Law in force on this day"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11(4): the power may be exercised in the way` `text V1` FALSE (YMD 2010 1 1) `in relation to all cases to which the power extends` FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 11(4) deals only where an enactment passed after 28th March 2003 confers a power to make any other enactment"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11(4): the power may be exercised in the way` `text V1` TRUE (YMD 2010 1 1) `in relation to all cases to which the power extends` TRUE
        BECAUSE "a contrary intention appears: Article 11(4) does not say how the power may then be exercised"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11(4): the power may be exercised in the way` `text inferred` TRUE (YMD 2010 1 1) `in relation to all cases to which the power extends` FALSE
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"

§ `Article 11A: the power to appoint to an office includes related powers (V2a to V2f only)`

`no circumstances` MEANS
    `Circumstances of an office` WITH
        `the office is vacant` IS FALSE
        `the person holding the office has been removed or suspended from office` IS FALSE
        `the person holding the office is absent temporarily or permanently` IS FALSE
        `the person holding the office is incapacitated in a way that affects the person's performance` IS FALSE

GIVEN vacant IS A BOOLEAN
      removed IS A BOOLEAN
      absent IS A BOOLEAN
      incapacitated IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Circumstances of an office`
`circumstances` vacant removed absent incapacitated MEANS
    `Circumstances of an office` WITH
        `the office is vacant` IS vacant
        `the person holding the office has been removed or suspended from office` IS removed
        `the person holding the office is absent temporarily or permanently` IS absent
        `the person holding the office is incapacitated in a way that affects the person's performance` IS incapacitated

#ASSERT `Article 11A: the power to appoint to an office includes the power` `text V2a` TRUE `to determine the terms and conditions of appointment` `no circumstances` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 11A: the power to appoint to an office includes the power` `text V2b` TRUE `to determine the terms and conditions of appointment` `no circumstances` FALSE
